# MANUAL SPEC MUTANT r4-a05-mulc/01
# type: FuluBeaconState
# ops: encode
# spec: the size of a list of n fixed-size elements is n * size(element); a product past NMAX (or one that wraps) must be the marker
# fault: the bound is the marker divided by es (div(2^32 - 1, es)): a product in (NMAX, 2^32 - 1] is accepted
# why: the wrong one of the two limits
# file: src/obj.bend
# sym: mulc
--- a/src/obj.bend
+++ b/src/obj.bend
@@ -1767,3 +1767,3 @@
 # n * es for a fixed element size es: the product when it does not wrap and is at most NMAX, else the marker (docs/SIZE_LIMIT_DESIGN.md).
-def mulc(+n: U32, +es: U32) -> U32: pick(U32.is_le(n, U32.div(4294967264, es)), (n * es : U32), 4294967295)
+def mulc(+n: U32, +es: U32) -> U32: pick(U32.is_le(n, U32.div(4294967295, es)), (n * es : U32), 4294967295)
 
